Yolanda,<br />
<br />
Preliminary result from the Ellersby Kinnaird billing review, and it is not=
 the result I expected when I opened the 2012 file.<br />
<br />
The firm did what it promised in 2012. All 103 accounts on Schedule A were =
re-papered onto the revised agreement, moved to Wexbury, and there has not =
been a debit instruction on any of them in twelve years. On those accounts =
the compliance record is clean.<br />
<br />
The exposure is in the 264 accounts the firm acquired from a retiring advis=
er in Sewickley in 2015. Those clients came across on their prior adviser's=
 paper, which contains a fee-debit authorization, and the firm assigned rat=
her than replaced the agreements. It has been transmitting debit instructio=
ns on them since 2015. No surprise examination for any year.<br />
<br />
The 2012 undertaking says the firm will remediate "the accounts identified =
in Schedule A." A 2015 account is not on Schedule A and cannot be added to =
it. So whatever this is, it is not a breach of the undertaking, and anyone =
framing it that way is going to be told so in the first paragraph of the an=
swer.<br />
